  "narrative": {
    "story": "The 3940 replaced the 3450 (a 1981 perpetual calendar) and was itself replaced by the 5140 in 2006. Across two decades and four metals (J yellow, R rose, G white, P platinum), the 3940 was the standard Patek perpetual — a 36mm dress watch with a micro-rotor automatic (Patek's first), a moon phase, a day/date, and a leap-year indicator. The 3940G with the silver dial (025) is the most-cited variant.",
